invariant: INV-14
file: x25519_wide_ed25519.h
catches: dnssec_test
reason: ed25519_verify_hram accepts a key of small order, so a DNSKEY whose
  A is the identity makes R = B, S = 1 a valid signature of every message.
  RFC 8032 permits it and libsodium refuses it, and ed25519_verify.h
  states the refusal. bin/dnssec_test presents that forgery, and fails on
  this edit.

--- old
    if (fe_equal(a.x, FE_ZERO)) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
